  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "We use the notation $\\sin^2\\theta$ to mean $(\\sin\\theta)^2$, $\\cos^2\\theta$ to mean $(\\cos\\theta)^2$ and $\\tan^2\\theta$ to mean $(\\tan\\theta)^2$. This is the standard notation. Find the exact values of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^2 30^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac14$",
          "worked": "$$\\sin^2 30^\\circ=\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2=\\frac14$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2 30^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac34$",
          "worked": "$$\\cos^2 30^\\circ=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac34$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan^2 30^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac13$",
          "worked": "$$\\tan^2 30^\\circ=\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\right)^2=\\frac13$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^2 300^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac34$",
          "worked": "The related angle is $60^\\circ$; sine is negative in the fourth quadrant.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2 300^\\circ&=(-\\sin60^\\circ)^2\\\\\\sin^2 300^\\circ&=\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\tan^2 240^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3$",
          "worked": "The related angle is $60^\\circ$; tangent is positive in the third quadrant.\n$$\\tan^2 240^\\circ=(\\tan60^\\circ)^2=(\\sqrt3)^2=3$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2 210^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac34$",
          "worked": "The related angle is $30^\\circ$; cosine is negative in the third quadrant.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2 210^\\circ&=(-\\cos30^\\circ)^2\\\\\\cos^2 210^\\circ&=\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^2 225^\\circ+\\cos^2 225^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "Both ratios are negative, with related angle $45^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2 225^\\circ+\\cos^2 225^\\circ&=\\left(-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\right)^2+\\left(-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\right)^2\\\\\\sin^2 225^\\circ+\\cos^2 225^\\circ&=\\frac12+\\frac12=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q7-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^2 330^\\circ+\\cos^2 330^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "The related angle is $30^\\circ$; sine is negative and cosine positive.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2 330^\\circ+\\cos^2 330^\\circ&=\\left(-\\frac12\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2\\\\\\sin^2 330^\\circ+\\cos^2 330^\\circ&=\\frac14+\\frac34=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
